From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi846: Keep the VBLANK frame length when setting the exposure

The exposure control writes the frame length register too, lengthening
the frame when the exposure comes within 6 lines of it. It started from
the mode's default frame length, not from the one set through
V4L2_CID_VBLANK: every exposure update, which comes every few frames
under auto exposure, put the frame length back to the default and
undid a longer frame set for a lower frame rate. Start from height +
vblank.

The exposure limit allows up to 2 lines below the frame, so an
exposure in the top 4 lines still lengthens the frame by up to 4
lines, as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index d68412691..edd279563 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -1560,7 +1560,8 @@ static int hi846_set_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 
 	case V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE:
 		shutter = ctrl->val;
-		frame_len = hi846->cur_mode->frame_len;
+		/* The frame length set through V4L2_CID_VBLANK, not the mode's default */
+		frame_len = hi846->cur_mode->height + hi846->vblank->val;
 
 		if (shutter > frame_len - 6) { /* margin */
 			frame_len = shutter + 6;
